add("llm-as-annotator",
 "LLMs as Annotators and Coders: Reliability, Bias, Human-in-the-Loop",
 "Module 13 addresses the newest standard practice: using LLMs to label/code large corpora (sentiment, frames, relevance, stance, ideology, topic labels). It teaches prompt/codebook design, multiple sampling and aggregation, validation against human gold sets, reliability gates (Cohen's kappa), bias and stereotype risks, cost/latency trade-offs, and when to distill to a smaller classifier. Includes the human-in-the-loop pattern now required for publication-grade work.",
 3,
 ["LLM-based structured labeling (codebook-to-prompt)", "Zero-shot vs few-shot vs fine-tuned coding", "Reliability validation against human coders (kappa)", "Aggregation, self-consistency, temperature effects", "Bias, stereotype amplification, and logit/prompt sensitivity", "Distillation to cheap classifiers for scale"],
 ["C3 Design a prompt-based codebook for a coding task", "C4 Validate LLM labels against a human gold set and report kappa", "C5 Identify bias risks and mitigate with sampling and review"],
 ["Prompt engineering, structured output (JSON), self-consistency, batch APIs (OpenAI/Anthropic batch, VLLM/local), kappa agreement",
  "Distillation training (student model on LLM labels)"],
 "Cohen's kappa vs human coders, Krippendorff's alpha for multi-coder, F1 vs gold, consistency across prompt variants, cost per 1k items",
 "False confidence from high accuracy on easy items, bias on identity categories, prompt sensitivity, silent drift with model version updates, leakage of sensitive data into APIs",
 "LLM SDKs (OpenAI/Anthropic/open-source), DSPy-style optimization, Google Sheets/Excel for gold sets, kappa libraries",
 "Not applicable; this is a methods module that replaces manual annotation",
 "API pricing per token; local open models free but require hardware; reliability work requires human coder time",
 "Run a small coding task with LLM, human-code a 200-item gold set, report kappa, iterate prompts, then distill",
 "Gold set from an Indonesian social corpus (e.g. stance on an issue)",
 ["Tornberg, 'Best practices for text annotation with LLMs' (2024)", "Gilardi et al., 'LLMs outperform expert coders' (2024)", "Bermejo et al. (2025) LLMs vs outsourced crowd coders"],
 ["Schroeder et al. (2025) human-in-the-loop for subjective coding tasks", "Carlson (2025) LLM annotation in management research"],
 "2024-2026: LLM annotation went from novelty to expected practice with mandatory validation and bias checks; batch APIs and prompt optimization (DSPy) made it scalable",
 TXT_HW, "Code 10,000 Indonesian posts for stance on a policy issue using LLM + human validation and report reliability.", "Codebook + gold set + kappa report + distilled classifier"),

