 "Module 17 models how content spreads: cascade trees, classical epidemic models (SIS/SIR on networks), branching process and Hawkes/temporal point process models for bursts, influence versus homophily as competing explanations, and prediction of what will trend. It connects to platform design (recommender amplification) so students can separate organic spread from algorithmic distribution.",
 3,
 ["Cascades and retweet trees", "SIS/SIR epidemic models on networks", "Independent cascade / linear threshold (IC/LT)", "Hawkes and self-exciting point processes", "Trending prediction and early-burst detection", "Algorithmic amplification vs organic spread"],
 ["C3 Reconstruct cascades and compute structural virality", "C4 Fit a simple diffusion model and predict spread", "C5 Discuss recommender amplification as a confound"],
